    "created_at": "2016-06-06T17:58:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-06T17:58:48Z",
    "body": "See also #805. I'm not sure what the plan is here---do we need to formalize the \"default action\" concept perhaps, and call it \"legacy default action\", so that all the existing places the spec talks about \"default action\" are no longer undefined references?\n\nIt looks like @rbyers and @dtapuska are involved in trying to make Chrome match... some spec, not sure which, but at least the general agreement to try to remove as many synthetic click activations as possible.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
